# Claude Code host map

Every rule above applies here unchanged. The rules and every skill under `~/.claude/skills/` are shared with other agent hosts, so they name capabilities, not tools. Here, read each term as:

| Written | Here |
|---|---|
| load the `<name>` skill | `Skill` tool, `<name>`. A path inside it → `Read` `~/.claude/skills/<name>/<path>` |
| spawn, dispatch, a parallel dispatch | an `Agent` call per spawn. A parallel dispatch → all its `Agent` calls in one message |
| a role, a custom role | `subagent_type` set to that exact name. The role `task` is the agent named `task` |
| the spawn call's model and effort override | the `Agent` call's `model` and `effort` parameters. Pass neither |
| message an agent, resume it, list the agents | `SendMessage` to the agent's name. It resumes with its context intact. `ListAgents` for the roster |
| a subagent's returned report | the result of its `Agent` call |
| a structured question call, multi-select, recommended option | `AskUserQuestion`. At most 4 questions a call and 2 to 4 options each, so a fifth question goes in the next call. The recommended option goes first with "(Recommended)" on its label |
| a background process | `Bash` with `run_in_background`, `TaskStop` to end it |
| the browser tool | `mcp__playwright__*`, a headless browser that only `tester`, `uxui-designer`, and `uxui-design-review` carry. Any other agent, this session included, has no browser: dispatch one of those three |
| `/tmp/agent/`, a scratch script | the session scratchpad directory. `/tmp/agent/` stays valid |
| language-server diagnostics, a language-server rename | `LSP` tool when listed, else the repo's own type-check or lint command |
| the language's debugger | the debugger or REPL through `Bash` |
| the Expo MCP tools | `mcp__Expo__*` |
| permission rules, permission settings | `permissions` in `~/.claude/settings.json` and `.claude/settings*.json` |
| the project's MCP config | `.mcp.json` at the repo root |
| an agent definition, its model and effort | `~/.claude/agents/<name>.md` |
| live agent config | `~/.claude/settings.json`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `~/.claude/agents/`, and `~/.config/ai/AGENTS.md` |

## Subagents

- `general-purpose`, `claude`, `Explore`, and `Plan` are denied in `~/.claude/settings.json`. A call that names one, or omits `subagent_type`, fails. A skill or command that names one → use the role that fits its work.
- Never use `fork` for a role a skill names. A fork inherits this session's model and effort and carries none of the role's tool limits.
